  {
    "name": "edgeSwipe",
    "description": "A finger or a pen that went down within `gestures.edgePx` of an edge of the screen and moved at least `gestures.swipeMinPx` away from it, as on a phone: `edge` is where it started, `direction` the way it went. The frame takes that touch: the scene hears no pointerDown, pointerMove or pointerUp of it, so a slider under it stays as it was. A touch there that lifts, holds or moves along the edge instead is the scene's after all, with its pointerDown a little late. Not a mouse.",
    "canListen": true,
    "fields": [
